From 7e8c9e1be07232b45a262a5aa2d1d31306e5e5c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bill Hlavacek <hlavacek@lanl.gov>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:13:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] bngsim: sum the total propensity afresh once it falls far,
 and fire above 0

DirectSelector kept the total propensity as a running sum, Atot - oldA +
newA, and summed it afresh only when a pick ran past the last reaction.
A propensity added to a large total is rounded to that total's spacing,
and is not given back when the large term is taken off again. With A + B
-> C at kf from 1000 of each beside 0 -> D at 1e-6, the sum held 0 once
A and B were gone at kf = 1e5, so D never fired, and 1.907e-6 at kf =
1e4, so D fired at 1.9 times its rate (bngsim GH #1666). A pick that ran
past the last reaction did sum the propensities afresh, but
System::a_tot kept the stale total, and every later waiting time was
drawn from it. The sum goes astray without a fall too, where the
roundings fall the same way every time: one molecule flipping between
two reactions beside a fixed background lost 2.2e-16 a cycle, without
bound, and the reaction listed last loses from every pick what the sum
has lost.

The selector now sums Atot from each reaction's get_a() once it has
fallen below 2^-10 of the largest value it has held since it was last
summed, or below 0, or once it has taken 2^12 updates since then, as
RuleMonkey sums its own every 4096 events. Each update rounds the sum by
about an ulp of that peak, so where the total is read it is off by at
most about 2^-40 of its peak with every rounding the same way: 2^-40 of
a total near its peak, well below the 2^-32 to which a pick is drawn,
and 2^-30 of one at 2^-10 of it. update() only counts and keeps the
peak; the tests are made where the total is read, before a waiting time
is drawn (getAtotForDraw(), new in ReactionSelector, getAtot() by
default) and before a pick. Within a firing the total can dip and come
back, as when a molecule that carries nearly all of it leaves one
reaction before it joins the next, and a sum is a pass over every
reaction where a pick may stop at the first: tested in update(), it made
a model with one such molecule beside 300 reactions 25% slower. Tested
where the total is read, a sum comes once per 2^12 updates and once per
fall by a factor of 1024. Each is a pass over all N reactions, so a
model whose total keeps falling that far below its peak slows in
proportion to N: one A flipping at 1e6 and back at 1e-3, nearly every
other firing a fall, ran 1.8 times as long beside 1000 births at 1e-9 as
without the tests, and 17 times as long beside 10,000. The count alone
costs a pass per 4096 updates. A total that is not finite is never
summed afresh there, and is kept for the host to report.
System::getNextRxn takes a_tot from the selector after each pick.

stepTo, sim and singleStep fired nothing while a_tot was at or below
ATOT_TOLERANCE, 1e-9, a rate in the model's own time unit: 0 -> D at
5e-10 never fired, and 100 A decaying at 1e-10 stopped at 10, where the
total is 1e-9 (bngsim GH #1672). With the total kept close to its sum
they fire at any total above 0, and ATOT_TOLERANCE is gone. The selector
picks no reaction from a total that is not above 0: random(0) is 0,
which the first reaction passes with a propensity of 0. stepTo and sim
then draw again from the total the selector found.

This is RuleWorld/nfsim#123, fixed upstream by RuleWorld/nfsim#128,
merged as 7501f675, and written here against the pinned base. Upstream
makes the same test of the fall, below 2^-10 of the peak since the last
sum or below 0, sums afresh from the propensities the selector holds,
removes ATOT_TOLERANCE, picks nothing from a total that is not above 0,
and reads a_tot back after a pick. This carry diverges in four ways. It
also sums the total afresh every 4096 updates, which upstream lacks: at
7501f675 the running total on bngsim's
tests/data/nfsim/drifting_flip.xml still loses 2.2e-16 a cycle, and the
reaction listed last is lost. It keeps the peak at every update, not
only where the total is read. It also tests before a pick. And where a
pick finds nothing, stepTo draws again rather than going to the stopping
time, as the time-table breakpoints of
bngsim/carry-step-to-time-table-breakpoints need, and sim draws again
where upstream lets the time pass. When the base moves past 7501f675,
reduce this carry to the count rather than drop it (bngsim GH #519).
---
 .../reactionSelector/directSelector.cpp       | 95 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../reactionSelector/reactionSelector.hh      | 18 ++++
 src/NFcore/system.cpp                         | 36 +++++--
 3 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/NFcore/reactionSelector/directSelector.cpp b/src/NFcore/reactionSelector/directSelector.cpp
index 5f75b1f..7383d45 100644
--- a/src/NFcore/reactionSelector/directSelector.cpp
+++ b/src/NFcore/reactionSelector/directSelector.cpp
@@ -9,10 +9,58 @@
 
 #include "reactionSelector.hh"
 
+#include <cmath>
+
 using namespace std;
 using namespace NFcore;
 
 
+/* update() keeps Atot as a running sum, Atot - oldA + newA. Each update rounds
+ * it twice, each time by at most about half an ulp of the largest value the sum
+ * has held since it was last summed, so n updates leave it off by up to about
+ * n * 2^-52 of that peak. A propensity added to a large total is rounded to the
+ * total's spacing, and is not given back when the large term is taken off
+ * again. A slow channel at 1e-6 beside a fast one at 1e11 was lost outright
+ * once the fast one was 0, and beside one at 1e10 it came back as 1.907e-6
+ * (bngsim GH #1666, RuleWorld/nfsim#123). The sum goes astray without a fall
+ * too, where the roundings fall the same way every time: one molecule flipping
+ * between two reactions beside a fixed background lost 2.2e-16 a cycle, and the
+ * reaction listed last loses from every pick what the sum has lost.
+ *
+ * So Atot is summed afresh once it has fallen below 2^-10 of that peak, or
+ * below 0, or once it has taken 2^12 updates since it was last summed, as
+ * RuleMonkey sums its own every 4096 events. Where it is read, it has then
+ * taken at most 2^12 updates more than one firing makes. With every rounding
+ * the same way, the case that drifts, that leaves it off by at most about
+ * 2^-40 of its peak. That is 2^-40 of a total near its peak, well below the
+ * 2^-32 of the total to which a pick is drawn (NfsimRNG::random), and 2^-30 of
+ * one that sits at 2^-10 of its peak. Where the roundings fall either way, it
+ * is about 2^-46 and 2^-36.
+ *
+ * update() only counts and keeps the peak. The tests are made where the total
+ * is read: before a waiting time is drawn from it (getAtotForDraw()) and before
+ * a pick. Within a firing the total can dip and come back, as when a molecule
+ * that carries nearly all of it leaves one reaction before it joins the next. A
+ * sum is a pass over every reaction, where a pick stops at the one it draws, so
+ * a test in update() would cost such a model a pass per firing. Where the total
+ * is read, a sum comes once per 2^12 updates and once per fall by a factor of
+ * 1024. Each is a pass over all N reactions, so a model whose total keeps
+ * falling that far below its peak slows in proportion to N. One A flipping at
+ * 1e6 and back at 1e-3, so that nearly every other firing is such a fall, ran
+ * 1.8 times as long beside 1000 births at 1e-9 as without the tests, and 17
+ * times as long beside 10,000. The count alone costs a pass per 4096 updates.
+ *
+ * RuleWorld/nfsim#128, merged upstream as 7501f675, makes the same test of the
+ * fall, before a waiting time is drawn, and has no count.
+ *
+ * The sum reads each reaction's get_a(), the propensities the running sum is
+ * made of, rather than computing every rate again as refactorPropensities()
+ * does.
+ *
+ * A total that is not finite is never summed afresh here: it is the model's
+ * own, and the host reports it. */
+static const double ATOT_RESUM_FRACTION = 1.0 / 1024.0;   // 2^-10
+static const unsigned int ATOT_RESUM_UPDATES = 4096;      // 2^12
 
 
 DirectSelector::DirectSelector(vector <ReactionClass *> &rxns, System *sys) :
@@ -25,6 +73,7 @@ DirectSelector::DirectSelector(vector <ReactionClass *> &rxns, System *sys) :
 		reactionClassList[r] = rxns.at(r);
 		Atot += reactionClassList[r]->get_a();
 	}
+	markSummed();
 }
 
 
@@ -42,6 +91,39 @@ double DirectSelector::refactorPropensities()
 	for(int r=0; r<n_reactions; r++) {
 		Atot += reactionClassList[r]->update_a();
 	}
+	markSummed();
+	return Atot;
+}
+
+
+void DirectSelector::resumPropensities()
+{
+	Atot = 0;
+	for(int r=0; r<n_reactions; r++) {
+		Atot += reactionClassList[r]->get_a();
+	}
+	markSummed();
+}
+
+
+void DirectSelector::markSummed()
+{
+	AtotPeak = Atot > 0 ? Atot : 0;
+	AtotResumBelow = AtotPeak * ATOT_RESUM_FRACTION;
+	updatesSinceSum = 0;
+}
+
+
+void DirectSelector::resumIfStale()
+{
+	if(!std::isfinite(Atot)) return;
+	if(Atot < AtotResumBelow || updatesSinceSum >= ATOT_RESUM_UPDATES) resumPropensities();
+}
+
+
+double DirectSelector::getAtotForDraw()
+{
+	resumIfStale();
 	return Atot;
 }
 
@@ -50,6 +132,11 @@ double DirectSelector::update(ReactionClass *r,double oldA, double newA)
 {
 	Atot-=oldA;
 	Atot+=newA;
+	++updatesSinceSum;
+	if(Atot > AtotPeak) {
+		AtotPeak = Atot;
+		AtotResumBelow = AtotPeak * ATOT_RESUM_FRACTION;
+	}
 	return Atot;
 }
 
@@ -57,6 +144,14 @@ double DirectSelector::update(ReactionClass *r,double oldA, double newA)
 
 double DirectSelector::getNextReactionClass(ReactionClass *&rc)
 {
+	resumIfStale();
+	// Nothing fires at a total of 0, or one that is not a number. random(0) is
+	// 0, which the first reaction would pass below with a propensity of 0; a
+	// pick that passed every reaction sums them afresh and comes back here.
+	if(!(Atot > 0)) {
+		rc = 0;
+		return 0;
+	}
 	double randNum = sys_->getRNG().random(Atot);
 
 	double a_sum=0, last_a_sum=0;
diff --git a/src/NFcore/reactionSelector/reactionSelector.hh b/src/NFcore/reactionSelector/reactionSelector.hh
index 9913aed..d8b011b 100644
--- a/src/NFcore/reactionSelector/reactionSelector.hh
+++ b/src/NFcore/reactionSelector/reactionSelector.hh
@@ -39,6 +39,9 @@ namespace NFcore
 			virtual double update(ReactionClass *r,double oldA, double newA) = 0;
 			virtual double getNextReactionClass(ReactionClass *&rc) = 0;
 			virtual double getAtot() = 0;
+			/* The total to draw a waiting time from. A selector that keeps a
+			 * running total may sum it afresh first. */
+			virtual double getAtotForDraw() { return getAtot(); }
 
 		protected:
 			System *sys_;  // Pointer to System for accessing per-instance RNG
@@ -58,10 +61,25 @@ namespace NFcore
 			virtual double update(ReactionClass *r,double oldA, double newA);
 			virtual double getNextReactionClass(ReactionClass *&rc);
 			virtual double getAtot();
+			virtual double getAtotForDraw();
 
 
 		protected:
+			/* Sums Atot afresh from the propensity each reaction holds. */
+			void resumPropensities();
+			/* Starts the watch on Atot that has it summed again. */
+			void markSummed();
+			/* Sums Atot afresh if it has fallen far, or taken many updates,
+			 * since it was last summed. */
+			void resumIfStale();
+
 			double Atot;
+			/* The largest value Atot has held since it was last summed, and
+			 * the value below which it is summed again. */
+			double AtotPeak;
+			double AtotResumBelow;
+			/* The updates Atot has taken since it was last summed. */
+			unsigned int updatesSinceSum;
 			int n_reactions;
 			ReactionClass ** reactionClassList;
 
diff --git a/src/NFcore/system.cpp b/src/NFcore/system.cpp
index 9b1c910..8c2e5c4 100644
--- a/src/NFcore/system.cpp
+++ b/src/NFcore/system.cpp
@@ -18,8 +18,6 @@
 #include "../NFscheduler/NFstream.h"
 #include "../NFscheduler/Scheduler.h"
 
-#define ATOT_TOLERANCE 1e-9
-
 using namespace std;
 using namespace NFcore;
 
@@ -960,8 +958,14 @@ double System::getNextRxn()
 		// Upstream NFsim v1.14.3 consumes and discards the first selector draw
 		// here, then uses the second draw/residual. Keep this only as an
 		// explicit compatibility mode for same-seed parity with that CLI.
-		return selector->getNextReactionClass(nextReaction);
-	}
+		x = selector->getNextReactionClass(nextReaction);
+	}
+	// The selector sums the propensities afresh at a pick from a total that
+	// has fallen far or taken many updates since it was last summed, or at a
+	// draw past the last reaction, and picks from that sum, which a_tot then
+	// follows, so the next waiting time is drawn from it (bngsim GH #1666).
+	// With nothing to fire there it picks no reaction.
+	a_tot = selector->getAtot();
 	return x;
 
 
@@ -1023,7 +1027,10 @@ double System::sim(double duration, long int sampleTimes, bool verbose)
 		//   dt = -ln(rand) / a_tot;
 		//Choose a random number on the OPEN interval (0,1) so that we never
 		//have a dt=0 or a dt=infinity
-		if(a_tot>ATOT_TOLERANCE) delta_t = -log(rng_.random_open()) / a_tot;
+		// Summed afresh first if it has fallen far or taken many updates
+		// (bngsim GH #1666).
+		a_tot = selector->getAtotForDraw();
+		if(a_tot>0) delta_t = -log(rng_.random_open()) / a_tot;
 		else { delta_t=0; current_time=end_time; }
 		if(DEBUG) cout<<"   Determine dt : " << delta_t << endl;
 
@@ -1078,6 +1085,9 @@ double System::sim(double duration, long int sampleTimes, bool verbose)
 		//4: Select next reaction class based on smallest j,
 		//   such that sum of a_j over all j >= r2*a_tot
 		double randElement = getNextRxn();
+		// The selector found nothing to fire in the propensities summed
+		// afresh: draw again from the total it found.
+		if(nextReaction == NULL) continue;
 		
 		if(DEBUG && verbose && iteration < 5) {
 			cout << "Selected: " << (nextReaction ? nextReaction->getName() : "NULL") << endl;
@@ -1505,7 +1515,14 @@ double System::stepTo(double stoppingTime)
 		if(!pendingStepEventValid) {
 			// Preserve the pending waiting-time draw across output boundaries so
 			// repeated stepTo() calls consume the same RNG stream as sim().
-			if(a_tot > ATOT_TOLERANCE) {
+			// Any total above 0 has a reaction to fire: read for the draw, the
+			// selector sums the propensities afresh where rounding could have
+			// left a_tot far from their sum (bngsim GH #1666), and it picks
+			// nothing where that sum is 0. A threshold of 1e-9 here, a rate in
+			// the model's own time unit, fired nothing in a model whose total
+			// was that small (bngsim GH #1672).
+			a_tot = selector->getAtotForDraw();
+			if(a_tot > 0.0) {
 				pendingStepEventTime =
 					current_time + (-log(rng_.random_open()) / a_tot);
 				pendingStepEventValid = true;
@@ -1535,8 +1552,11 @@ double System::stepTo(double stoppingTime)
 		// Select and fire the next reaction
 		double randElement = getNextRxn();
 		if(nextReaction == NULL) {
+			// The selector found nothing to fire in the propensities summed
+			// afresh, so the waiting time was drawn from a stale total: draw
+			// again from the total it found.
 			invalidateStepToCache();
-			break;
+			continue;
 		}
 
 		current_time = pendingStepEventTime;
@@ -1566,7 +1586,7 @@ void System::singleStep()
 
 	recompute_A_tot();
 	cout<<"  -total propensity (a_total) calculated as: "<<a_tot<<endl;
-	if(a_tot>ATOT_TOLERANCE) delta_t = -log(rng_.random_open()) / a_tot;
+	if(a_tot>0) delta_t = -log(rng_.random_open()) / a_tot;
 	else
 	{
 		//Otherwise, we can't react for the rest of this step
